<title>USA: Leucadia says it remains in talks for sale.</title>
<headline>Leucadia says it remains in talks for sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leucadia National Corp said Wednesday it remains in talks about the sale of some of its insurance operations.</p>
<p>It could not provide any more details.</p>
<p>The company said it made the announcement in response to to news of its sale of Colonial Penn Life Insurance Co, Providential Life Insurance Co and other assets to Conseco Inc for $460 million in cash and notes.</p>
<p>The company added that it is authorized by its board of directors to buy back up to 2.260 million of its common shares.</p>
</text>
